  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forest Guard Training for Conservation of Hoolock gibbon in the state of Arunachal Pradesh, India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will accomplish the following objectives to help conserve endangered western hoolock gibbons and their habitats in Arunachal Pradesh: (1) Educate, and inculcate interest in Forest Guards to protect hoolock gibbon habitats, and educate them about global, national and local importance of the species; (2) Train Forest Guards to identify the different primate species, and classify individuals based on age and sex to facilitate individual identification to maintain individual histories; (3) Teach and train the Forest Guards about general primate survey, hoolock gibbon population estimates and the present status of Hoolock gibbons; (4) Train them about legal provisions in the Wildlife Act as well as wildlife laws to reduce wildlife crimes; (5) Sensitize field staff about the value and ethics of wildlife conservation and bio-diversity propagation by bringing about an attitudinal change among forest staff and the local community.</narrative>
  </description>
